Ideas that nobody has got round to yet.  Concrete bugs and requests live
in the issue tracker: https://github.com/autotrace/autotrace/issues

Tracing:
- Recognise circle and ellipse pieces.
- Recognise lines, splines and circles in noisy input.
- Trace and fit every outline only once (outlines are currently traced
  twice, which is slow and leaves unwanted gaps).
- A better thinning algorithm for -centerline, e.g. the Chordal Axis
  Transform.
- An algorithm that copes with anti-aliased input.
- Images have to fit completely into memory.

Output:
- More formats: WMF, CDR, CMX, compressed PDF and SVG, DXF with splines.

Library and its clients:
- A maintained graphical front end (frontline is inactive).
- A predefined parameter (preset) system.
- Report errors through GError instead of at_exception.
